{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion (RNA + image) meaningfully improves accuracy over single-modality baselines, and which encoder combination is strongest. config_005 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion) directly tests this core hypothesis using a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) and a strong pretrained image encoder (ViT-L) with a simple concat fusion. It avoids the added cost of multiprofile aggregation, keeping training time moderate (estimated medium cost: ViT-L is the main expense, but single-profile and no aggregation module keep it well below the multiprofile+transformer configs). A strong result here establishes a high-accuracy reference and justifies investing later experiments in multiprofile aggregation and transformer fusion; a weak result would redirect exploration toward single-modality or alternative encoders. This is the best use of experiment 1 because it maximally reduces uncertainty about the central design axis (multimodal vs. unimodal, and encoder quality) while remaining cost-efficient enough to leave budget for follow-up exploitation."
}

